    <!-- About -->
    <string name="about_privacy_body">Pingu Messages has no servers. Your messages stay in Android\'s own message store on this phone. Nothing is uploaded, there is no analytics, and there are no third-party trackers in the app.</string>
    <string name="limitation_rcs_title">RCS chat features</string>
    <string name="limitation_rcs_body">RCS on Android runs through Google\'s Jibe infrastructure, which is not open to other apps. Pingu Messages therefore does not claim to support RCS: it implements SMS and MMS properly instead, and its transport layer is built so another protocol could be added if one ever becomes available to third-party apps.</string>
    <string name="limitation_reactions_title">Reactions</string>
    <string name="limitation_reactions_body">SMS and MMS have no reaction field. Reactions you add are stored on this phone. If you turn on \"Send reactions as text\", a short message is also sent so the other person sees it — that is exactly what iPhone and Google Messages do when they fall back to SMS. Reactions other people send that way are recognised and shown on the right message rather than as a confusing extra line.</string>
    <string name="limitation_edit_title">Editing a sent message</string>
    <string name="limitation_edit_body">Once a text message reaches the network it cannot be changed or recalled — there is no mechanism in SMS to do it. You can edit a scheduled message before it goes out, and edit and resend one that failed.</string>
    <string name="limitation_delete_title">Deleting for everyone</string>
    <string name="limitation_delete_body">Deleting a message removes it from this phone. Nothing can remove it from the recipient\'s phone; any app claiming otherwise for SMS is not telling the truth.</string>
    <string name="limitation_read_title">Read receipts</string>
    <string name="limitation_read_body">SMS has no read receipt at all, so this app never shows one. Delivery reports are real and can be turned on in Settings, though some carriers charge for them. MMS does support read reports, and those are shown when the other phone sends one.</string>
    <string name="limitation_typing_title">Typing indicators</string>
    <string name="limitation_typing_body">There is no typing indicator in SMS or MMS. Nothing in this app pretends to show one.</string>
    <string name="limitation_encryption_title">Encryption</string>
    <string name="limitation_encryption_body">SMS and MMS are not end-to-end encrypted; they travel through your carrier in the clear. No app can change that. On this phone your messages live in Android\'s own message store, protected by the device encryption your lock screen enables.</string>

